 Manual page screen(1) line 12 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBBGETTING STARTED
 Manual page screen(1) line 13 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       Before you begin to use screen you'll need to make sure you have correctly selected your terminal type, just as you
 Manual page screen(1) line 14 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       would for any other termcap/terminfo program.  (You can do this by using test for example.)
 Manual page screen(1) line 15 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB
 Manual page screen(1) line 16 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       If you're impatient and want to get started without doing a lot more reading, you should remember this one command:
 Manual page screen(1) line 17 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       C-a ?.  Typing these two characters will display a list of the available screen commands and their  bindings.  Each
 Manual page screen(1) line 18 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       keystroke  is  discussed  in the section DEFAULT KEY BINDINGS. The manual section CUSTOMIZATION deals with the con
 Manual page screen(1) line 19 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       tents of your .screenrc.
 Manual page screen(1) line 20 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB
 Manual page screen(1) line 21 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       If your terminal is a true auto-margin terminal (it doesn't allow the last position on the  screen  to  be  updated
 Manual page screen(1) line 22 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       without scrolling the screen) consider using a version of your terminal's termcap that has automatic margins turned
 Manual page screen(1) line 23 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       off. This will ensure an accurate and optimal update of the screen in all circumstances.  Most  terminals  nowadays
 Manual page screen(1) line 24 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       have  magic  margins (automatic margins plus usable last column). This is the VT100 style type and perfectly suited
 Manual page screen(1) line 25 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       for screen.  If all you've got is a true auto-margin terminal screen will be content to  use  it,  but  updating  a
 Manual page screen(1) line 26 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       character put into the last position on the screen may not be possible until the screen scrolls or the character is
 Manual page screen(1) line 27 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       moved into a safe position in some other way. This delay can be shortened by using a terminal with insert-character
 Manual page screen(1) line 28 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       capability.
 Manual page screen(1) line 29 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB
 Manual page screen(1) line 30 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBBCOMMAND-LINE OPTIONS
 Manual page screen(1) line 31 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       Screen has the following command-line options:
 Manual page screen(1) line 32 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB
 Manual page screen(1) line 33 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       -a   include  all  capabilities  (with  some minor exceptions) in each window's termcap, even if screen must redraw
 Manual page screen(1) line 34 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB            parts of the display in order to implement a function.
 Manual page screen(1) line 35 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB
 Manual page screen(1) line 36 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       -A   Adapt the sizes of all windows to the size of the current terminal.  By default, screen tries to  restore  its
 Manual page screen(1) line 37 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB            old  window sizes when attaching to resizable terminals (those with WS in its description, e.g. suncmd or some
 Manual page screen(1) line 38 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB            xterm).
 Manual page screen(1) line 39 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB
 Manual page screen(1) line 40 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       -c file
 Manual page screen(1) line 41 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB            override the default configuration file from $HOME/.screenrc to file.
 Manual page screen(1) line 42 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB
 Manual page screen(1) line 43 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       -d|-D [pid.tty.host]
 Manual page screen(1) line 44 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB            does not start screen, but detaches the elsewhere running screen session. It has the same effect as typing C-a
 Manual page screen(1) line 45 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB            d  from screen's controlling terminal. -D is the equivalent to the power detach key.  If no session can be de
 Manual page screen(1) line 46 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB            tached, this option is ignored. In combination with the -r/-R option more powerful effects can be achieved:
 Manual page screen(1) line 47 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB
 Manual page screen(1) line 48 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       -d -r   Reattach a session and if necessary detach it first.
 Manual page screen(1) line 49 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB
 Manual page screen(1) line 50 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       -d -R   Reattach a session and if necessary detach or even create it first.
 Manual page screen(1) line 51 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB
 Manual page screen(1) line 52 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       -d -RR  Reattach a session and if necessary detach or create it. Use the first session if more than one session  is
 Manual page screen(1) line 53 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB               available.
 Manual page screen(1) line 54 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB
 Manual page screen(1) line 55 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       -D -r   Reattach a session. If necessary detach and logout remotely first.
 Manual page screen(1) line 56 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB
 Manual page screen(1) line 57 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       -D -R   Attach  here and now. In detail this means: If a session is running, then reattach. If necessary detach and
 Manual page screen(1) line 58 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB               logout remotely first.  If it was not running create it and notify the user. This is the author's favorite.
 Manual page screen(1) line 59 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB
 Manual page screen(1) line 60 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       -D -RR  Attach here and now. Whatever that means, just do it.
 Manual page screen(1) line 61 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB
 Manual page screen(1) line 62 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB            Note: It is always a good idea to check the status of your sessions by means of screen -list.
 Manual page screen(1) line 63 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB
 Manual page screen(1) line 64 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB       -e xy
