 Manual page screen(1) line 88 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB            does not start screen, but prints a list of pid.tty.host strings  and  creation  timestamps  identifying  your
 Manual page screen(1) line 89 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB            screen  sessions.   Sessions marked `detached' can be resumed with screen -r. Those marked `attached' are run
 Manual page screen(1) line 90 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB            ning and have a controlling terminal. If the session runs in multiuser mode, it is  marked  `multi'.  Sessions
 Manual page screen(1) line 91 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB            marked  as  `unreachable' either live on a different host or are `dead'.  An unreachable session is considered
 Manual page screen(1) line 92 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB            dead, when its name matches either the name of the local host, or the specified parameter, if any.  See the -r
 Manual page screen(1) line 93 (press h for help or q to quit) ESCESCOOBB            flag  for  a description how to construct matches.  Sessions marked as `dead' should be thoroughly checked and
